.\" Transom 手册页：安装包内的 usr/share/man/man1/transom.1。
.\" 为什么用英文：桌面条目的 GenericName 与包控制字段同为系统级英文资产，
.\" 与 README.md（英文主文件）口径一致；中文用户文档由 README_zh-CN.md 承担。
.TH TRANSOM 1 "2026-10-28" "Transom 1.2.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
transom \- native SSH, serial console and terminal workspace with integrated SFTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B transom
.RI [ ssh:// [ user@ ] host [ :port ]]...
.RI [ \-\-dir= DIRECTORY ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B transom
is a desktop operations client: SSH and serial\-console sessions, local shells
and Telnet, with an SFTP file panel, port forwarding, snippet library, command
history, and optional per\-connection audit logging, rendered natively on GPUI
with no embedded web view.
.PP
Launching
.B transom
while an instance is already running does not start a second process: the
request is handed to the running instance over a private socket
.RB ( $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/transom ,
directory 0700, socket 0600) and new tabs open in the existing window.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.BI ssh:// [user@]host[:port]
Connect to
.I host
without saving a session, in a new tab. More than one URL may be given; each
opens its own tab. The scheme is matched case\-insensitively.
.TP
.BI \-\-dir= DIRECTORY
Open a new local terminal tab in
.IR DIRECTORY .
The directory must exist and be an absolute path; relative forms and
non\-existent paths are ignored with a log entry. The two\-argument form
.B \-\-dir
.I DIRECTORY
is also accepted.
.TP
.I DIRECTORY
A bare absolute\-path positional argument is treated as a directory request,
equivalent to
.BR \-\-dir .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TRANSOM_LOG
Log level override for this run
.RB ( trace ", " debug ", " info ", " warn ", " error ).
.B RUST_LOG
is honoured as a fallback. Either variable wins over the level saved in
settings; the default level is
.BR info .
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/transom/sessions.json
Session tree and connection settings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/transom/settings.json
Preferences, theme, fonts, shortcuts, snippets.
.TP
.I ~/.config/transom/known_hosts.json
Host key fingerprints (trust\-on\-first\-use).
.TP
.I ~/.config/transom/logs/
Application log with size\-based rotation (5 MiB per file, four backups).
.TP
.I ~/.config/transom/audit/
Optional per\-connection raw output capture; off by default.
.TP
.I OS keyring, service "transom"
Passwords and key passphrases; never written to disk by Transom.
.PP
On macOS paths follow the platform conventions
.RB ( "~/Library/Application Support/transom" ).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh_config (5)
